{
  "slug": "plausibleba-business-architecture-skills",
  "name": "Plausibleba Business Architecture Skills",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Methodology-grade business architecture for Claude. Four slash commands that elicit, validate, and visualise a complete business architecture from any business description, no templates or prior models needed.\n\n/plausibleba - Guided session producing a Capability Map, Concept Model, and Value Stream in one flow. Exports a single ba-skills-bundle.json.\n\n/capability-map - BIZBOK-grounded MECE capability hierarchy (L1–L3) with interactive treemap. Auto-generates XLSX and JSON exports.\n\n/concept-model - Business object taxonomy using the Capsicum Triad (Party/Record/Resource). Cross-validates against capability coverage.\n\n/value-stream - Staged value delivery with outcome chains, PPIT breakdown, and capability alignment.\n\nEach skill includes two validation checkpoints before rendering, auto-generated XLSX/JSON downloads, and recommended next steps to run companion skills.\n\nOpen source at github.com/plausibleba/ba-skills.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (2): `ba-capability-mapping` (Use this skill whenever a business analyst, architect, or project team needs to produce a Capability Map —…), `ba-taxonomy-standard` (Shared conventions used across all PlausibleBA skills)\n- **Commands** (1): `capability-map`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install plausibleba-business-architecture-skills@claude-community` from `plausibleba/ba-skills`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
